// JSON, parsed and printed by walking itself.
//
// A value holds its children in a `series of jval` — a series is a reference, so the struct
// closes and the type is finite. The same shape as an expression tree: `kind` says which of the
// other fields carries the answer, and both walks dispatch on it.
//
// The parser functions live at the TOP LEVEL rather than inside the rabbit, because parse-value
// and parse-array call each other. A Bind nested in a block is a closure the compiler emits
// where it stands, so neither of a mutually recursive pair could come first; top-level functions
// are hoisted and both backends agree.

Define object jval with (the text kind, the number num, the text str, the series of jval items).

// What a parse produced, and where it stopped. A function returns one thing, so the two travel
// together — a caller needs the cursor to know where to carry on from.
Define object parsed with (the jval value, the number cursor).

Bind text to char-at, given (the text source, the number cursor):
    If cursor is less than 1, return "".
    If cursor is greater than the length of source, return "".
    Return the characters from cursor to cursor of source.
Done.

Bind number to skip-spaces, given (the text source, the number cursor):
    Define spot as cursor.
    While cast char-at on (source, spot) is " ", repeat:
        The spot becomes spot + 1.
    Done.
    Return spot.
Done.

Bind fact to is-digit, given (the text letter):
    If letter is "0" or letter is "1" or letter is "2" or letter is "3", return true.
    If letter is "4" or letter is "5" or letter is "6" or letter is "7", return true.
    If letter is "8" or letter is "9", return true.
    Return false.
Done.

Bind jval to make-leaf, given (the text kind, the number num, the text str):
    Return a new jval { the kind kind, the num num, the str str, the items a series of jval }.
Done.

Bind parsed to parse-text, given (the text source, the number cursor):
    Define spot as cursor + 1.                       // step over the opening quote
    Define gathered as "".
    While cast char-at on (source, spot) is not "\"", repeat:
        The gathered becomes "{gathered}{cast char-at on (source, spot)}".
        The spot becomes spot + 1.
    Done.
    Return a new parsed { the value cast make-leaf on ("str", 0, gathered), the cursor spot + 1 }.
Done.

Bind parsed to parse-number, given (the text source, the number cursor):
    Define spot as cursor.
    Define gathered as "".
    If cast char-at on (source, spot) is "-":
        The gathered becomes "-".
        The spot becomes spot + 1.
    Done.
    While cast is-digit on (cast char-at on (source, spot)), repeat:
        The gathered becomes "{gathered}{cast char-at on (source, spot)}".
        The spot becomes spot + 1.
    Done.
    Define amount as gathered converted to number but void is 0.
    Return a new parsed { the value cast make-leaf on ("num", amount, ""), the cursor spot }.
Done.

Bind parsed to parse-array, given (the text source, the number cursor):
    Define spot as cast skip-spaces on (source, cursor + 1).      // step over '['
    Define gathered as a series of jval.
    While cast char-at on (source, spot) is not "]", repeat:
        Define outcome as cast parse-value on (source, spot).
        Add the value of outcome to gathered.
        The spot becomes cast skip-spaces on (source, the cursor of outcome).
        If cast char-at on (source, spot) is ",", spot becomes cast skip-spaces on (source, spot + 1).
    Done.
    Define holder as a new jval { the kind "array", the num 0, the str "", the items gathered }.
    Return a new parsed { the value holder, the cursor spot + 1 }.
Done.

Bind parsed to parse-value, given (the text source, the number cursor):
    Define spot as cast skip-spaces on (source, cursor).
    Define letter as cast char-at on (source, spot).
    If letter is "[", return cast parse-array on (source, spot).
    If letter is "\"", return cast parse-text on (source, spot).
    If letter is "t", return a new parsed { the value cast make-leaf on ("true", 0, ""), the cursor spot + 4 }.
    If letter is "f", return a new parsed { the value cast make-leaf on ("false", 0, ""), the cursor spot + 5 }.
    If letter is "n", return a new parsed { the value cast make-leaf on ("null", 0, ""), the cursor spot + 4 }.
    Return cast parse-number on (source, spot).
Done.

Bind text to render, given (the jval value):
    If the kind of value is "null", return "null".
    If the kind of value is "true", return "true".
    If the kind of value is "false", return "false".
    If the kind of value is "num", return the num of value converted to text.
    If the kind of value is "str", return "\"{the str of value}\"".
    If the kind of value is "array":
        Define out as "[".
        Define leading as true.
        For each kid in the items of value, repeat:
            If leading is false, out becomes "{out},".
            The out becomes "{out}{cast render on (kid)}".
            The leading becomes false.
        Done.
        Return "{out}]".
    Done.
    Return "?".
Done.

Pull a rabbit.
    // Each of these is parsed into a tree and printed back out, so what you see is the round
    // trip rather than the input echoed. Spacing disappears because the printer never adds any.
    Define documents as a series of text with (
        "[1, \"hi\", true, null, [2, -3], false]",
        "[]",
        "[[], [[1]]]",
        "  [ 1 , 2 ]  ",
        "[\"héllo 👍\"]").

    For each document in documents, repeat:
        Define outcome as cast parse-value on (document, 1).
        State cast render on (the value of outcome).
    Done.
Done.
